  TITLE     ONECUT2 is a targetable master regulator of lethal prostate cancer
            that suppresses the androgen axis
  JOURNAL   Nat. Med. 24 (12), 1887-1898 (2018)
   PUBMED   30478421
  REMARK    GeneRIF: Here we identify the transcription factor ONECUT2 (OC2) as
            a master regulator of AR networks in metastatic
            castration-resistant prostate cancer (mCRPC). OC2 acts as a
            survival factor in mCRPC models, suppresses the AR transcriptional
            program by direct regulation of AR target genes and the AR
            licensing factor FOXA1, and activates genes associated with neural
            differentiation and progression to lethal disease.
