COMMENT     REVIEWED REFSEQ: This record has been curated by NCBI staff. The
            reference sequence was derived from X17254.1 and AI057349.1.
            
            On Aug 31, 2019 this sequence version replaced NM_002049.3.
            
            Summary: This gene encodes a protein which belongs to the GATA
            family of transcription factors. The protein plays an important
            role in erythroid development by regulating the switch of fetal
            hemoglobin to adult hemoglobin. Mutations in this gene have been
            associated with X-linked dyserythropoietic anemia and
            thrombocytopenia. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008].
            
            Publication Note:  This RefSeq record includes a subset of the
            publications that are available for this gene. Please see the Gene
            record to access additional publications.
            
